\n**E002 body:**\n\n# FIPS crypto remediation for KServe control-plane and data-plane images\n\n## Description\n\nReplace non-validated cryptographic library usage in KServe-owned serving-stack\nimages so the model serving stack runs correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\nclusters using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated crypto in the\nrequest path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Identify non-validated crypto usage across KServe control-plane and\n  data-plane images: the controller, inference service data-plane containers\n  (predictor, transformer, explainer), queue proxy, storage initializer, and\n  router\n- Remediate each affected image: switch to validated crypto modules and\n  FIPS-compatible builds/base images\n- Rebuild the remediated images and validate the serving stack on a FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift cluster (both serverless and raw deployment modes where applicable)\n- Confirm no functional regression on non-FIPS clusters\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- No KServe-owned serving-stack image contains non-validated crypto in the\n  request path, verified by binary/library inspection of each image\n- InferenceService resources deploy and serve inference requests correctly on a\n  FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster (Ready status conditions reached; sample\n  inference requests succeed)\n- No functional regression on non-FIPS clusters\n- Build pipeline is green for all remediated images\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n  using validated crypto modules\n\n**E003 body:**\n\n# FIPS crypto remediation for Platform Operator images\n\n## Description\n\nRemediate non-validated cryptographic library usage in Platform Operator\nimages so the operator runs correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using\nvalidated crypto modules. Scope is determined by the validated findings on the\ncomponent's platform status, image set, and per-image crypto inventory.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Remediate each affected Platform Operator image per the confirmed inventory\n  and remediation recommendations: switch to validated crypto modules and\n  FIPS-compatible builds/base images\n- Rebuild the remediated images\n- Validate operator behavior on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster\n- Confirm no functional regression on non-FIPS clusters\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- No Platform Operator image contains non-validated crypto in the request path,\n  verified by binary/library inspection\n- The operator reconciles the serving stack correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift cluster\n- No functional regression on non-FIPS clusters\n- Build pipeline is green for all remediated images (per the component's\n  confirmed pipeline status)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n  using validated crypto modules\n\n**E004 body:**\n\n# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n\n## Description\n\nA gating CI check that fails any serving-stack build which reintroduces\nnon-validated crypto usage, enforcing FIPS compliance regressions in\ncontinuous integration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement a detection mechanism that identifies non-validated crypto usage in\n  built serving-stack images/binaries\n- Wire the check into the serving-stack build pipelines as a gating step\n- Fail builds on detection; report results clearly\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The check runs on every serving-stack build\n- A build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage fails the gate\n- The check passes on the remediated baseline\n- Gate results are visible in build output\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): CI enforces FIPS regressions with a gating check\n\n**E005 body:**\n\n# FIPS compliance evidence package and certification submission\n\n## Description\n\nAssemble the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the remediated model\nserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and\nsubmit it through the security review board to the external accredited\ncertification lab.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Produce the module inventory: validated crypto modules per serving-stack\n  image\n- Collect build attestations for all remediated images\n- Collect FIPS-mode test results (cluster validation results from the\n  remediation work)\n- Assemble the package in the format required by the security review board and\n  certification lab\n- Shepherd the package through security review board sign-off milestones and\n  submit to the external lab\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Module inventory covers every serving-stack image in scope\n- Build attestations exist for all remediated images\n- FIPS-mode test results are included\n- The package passes security review board sign-off at the defined milestones\n- The package is submitted to the external certification lab\n- Note: lab scheduling and review-board cadence are externally controlled and\n  cannot be compressed by engineering effort; timing is a schedule risk, not a\n  work-scope item\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): compliance evidence package assembled and submitted through the\n  security review board to the external certification lab\n\n**E006 body:**\n\n# Document FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites\n\n## Description\n\nDocumentation stating the FIPS support posture of the model serving stack and\nthe cluster prerequisites for running it on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Document the FIPS support posture: what is validated, what is not, and known\n  limitations\n- Document cluster prerequisites: FIPS-enabled OpenShift, required\n  configuration\n- Technical review of the content against the implemented remediation and\n  architecture context before publication\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Documentation states the FIPS support posture of the model serving stack\n- Cluster prerequisites for FIPS-enabled operation are documented\n- Content is technically reviewed against the implementation for accuracy\n-