{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acd996a2abb5eba5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition — RHAISTRAT-9013: FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tStep 0 checks did not fire. The strategy is not below-threshold: it spans two\n15\tcomponents (KServe, Platform Operator) and multiple architecturally distinct\n16\twork streams (image remediation, CI enforcement, compliance evidence assembly\n17\tand external submission, documentation). It is not documentation-only: image\n18\tand code changes are required. Full decomposition follows.\n19\t\n20\t## Parsed Strategy Structure\n21\t\n22\t- Affected Components: KServe, Platform Operator (no owner teams stated)\n23\t- HLRs: HLR-1 (P0, all serving-stack images run on FIPS-enabled clusters with\n24\t  validated crypto), HLR-2 (P0, compliance evidence package assembled and\n25\t  submitted through the security review board to the external certification\n26\t  lab), HLR-3 (P1, CI gating check for FIPS regressions), HLR-4 (P2,\n27\t  documentation of FIPS support posture)\n28\t- Out of scope: FIPS posture for workbenches/pipelines/training, Common\n29\t  Criteria certification\n30\t- Open questions: none on scope; lab scheduling and review-board cadence are\n31\t  externally controlled\n32\t\n33\tMissing sections (health warning): no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n34\ttable, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no Non-Functional Requirements,\n35\tno Staff Engineer Input. Decomposition proceeded with available information.\n36\t\n37\t## Component Mapping\n38\t\n39\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | In architecture context? | Notes |\n40\t|---|---|---|---|\n41\t| KServe | KServe | Yes (architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md) | Owning team RHOAI Serving; Konflux onboarded |\n42\t| Platform Operator | Platform Operator | No | In the canonical Jira component list but has no architecture context file — platform status unvalidated; Investigation E001 gates its remediation epic |\n43\t| (documentation work) | Documentation | n/a | HLR-4 docs epic uses the canonical Documentation component |\n44\t\n45\t## Epic List\n46\t\n47\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n48\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 | Validate Platform Operator platform status and FIPS remediation scope | Investigation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 | FIPS crypto remediation for KServe control-plane and data-plane images | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 | FIPS crypto remediation for Platform Operator images | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 | CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P1 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 | FIPS compliance evidence package and certification submission | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E006 | Document FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P0 |\n55\t\n56\t## Dependency DAG\n57\t\n58\tArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"E001 --> E003\" means E001 must\n59\tcomplete before E003 starts).\n60\t\n61\t```mermaid\n62\tgraph TD\n63\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: Platform Operator validation\"]\n64\t    E002[\"E002 Impl: KServe FIPS remediation\"]\n65\t    E003[\"E003 Impl: Platform Operator FIPS remediation\"]\n66\t    E004[\"E004 Impl: CI FIPS regression gate\"]\n67\t    E005[\"E005 Impl: Compliance evidence package\"]\n68\t    E006[\"E006 Docs: FIPS support posture\"]\n69\t    E001 --> E003\n70\t    E002 --> E004\n71\t    E002 --> E005\n72\t    E003 --> E005\n73\t    E002 --> E006\n74\t    E003 --> E006\n75\t    E004 --> E006\n76\t    E005 --> E006\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\t## DAG Justification\n80\t\n81\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n82\t|------|------|-----------|\n83\t| E001 → E003 | Step 2 new-component detection / Rule 3 | Platform Operator has no architecture context file; its platform status, image set, and crypto posture are unsubstantiated. The investigation's outcome rewrites or removes the remediation epic — a true gate (`rewrite`), recorded via `gated_by` on E003. The outcome space is an open-ended per-image inventory (not ≤3 bounded outcomes), so no conditional branch files; the gate carries a fallback approach instead. |\n84\t| E002 → E004 | Implementation ordering (gating semantics) | HLR-3 requires a *gating* check that fails builds that *reintroduce* non-validated crypto. Enabling it before a remediated baseline exists would fail every serving-stack build. This is a semantic ordering, not a Rule 15 merge-conflict coordination case. |\n85\t| E002 → E005 | Artifact dependency | The evidence package contains build attestations and test results for the remediated KServe images; it cannot be assembled before they exist. |\n86\t| E003 → E005 | Artifact dependency | Same, for the Platform Operator images in the evidence scope. |\n87\t| E002, E003, E004, E005 → E006 | Rule 11 | `docs-authoring` is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Per the docs-authoring priority exception these edges do not trigger priority inheritance. |\n88\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 | Different components/repos, no shared artifacts — KServe remediation starts immediately and is not gated by the Platform Operator validation. |\n89\t| (no edge) E004 ∥ E005 | Rule 14 | After their respective prerequisites, the CI regression gate and the evidence package share no artifact; the CI gate is not certification evidence. |\n90\t\n91\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n92\t\n93\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epics |\n94\t|-----|----------|------------------------|-------|\n95\t| HLR-1 | P0 | All serving-stack images run on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules | E002, E003 (gated by E001) |\n96\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Compliance evidence package assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab | E005 |\n97\t| HLR-3 | P1 | CI enforces FIPS regressions with a gating check | E004 |\n98\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites | E006 |\n99\t\n100\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n101\t\n102\t## Tiered Delivery\n103\t\n104\tThe external certification lab (six-to-nine-month historical turnaround) and\n105\tthe security review board cadence are third-party schedules that engineering\n106\tcannot compress. Partial value without certification: yes.\n107\t\n108\t- **Tier 1** (independent value): E001, E002, E003, E004 — the serving stack\n109\t  actually runs on FIPS-enabled clusters with validated crypto, and regressions\n110\t  are enforced in CI.\n111\t- **Tier 2** (externally gated): E005 — evidence package assembly and\n112\t  submission; the certification outcome and timing are externally controlled.\n113\t  The lab is a third party that resolves the certification itself, so it is\n114\t  modeled as a precondition/schedule risk on E005 (noted in its acceptance\n115\t  criteria), not as a separate epic.\n116\t\n117\t## Health Warnings\n118\t\n119\t1. **Missing strategy sections** — no Impacted Teams, Dependencies, Acceptance\n120\t   Criteria, or NFR sections. Team assignments for Platform Operator\n121\t   (\"RHOAI Platform\") and Documentation (\"RHOAI Documentation\") are assumptions;\n122\t   KServe's team (RHOAI Serving) comes from architecture context.\n123\t2. **Ambiguity — serving data plane scope**: the problem statement says \"KServe\n124\t   components and the serving data plane\" link non-validated crypto, and\n125\t   KServe's architecture context lists model-server runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO,\n126\t   Caikit) as its model-execution dependency. \"Serving Runtimes\" is NOT in the\n127\t   Affected Components table. The decomposition scopes the KServe epic to\n128\t   KServe-owned control-plane and data-plane images (controller,\n129\t   predictor/transformer/explainer, queue proxy, storage initializer, router).\n130\t   If model-server runtime images are intended to be in scope for HLR-1 (\"all\n131\t   serving-stack images\"), the strategy needs an amendment — they sit in the\n132\t   request path per architecture context.\n133\t3. **Priority note — docs epic**: HLR-4 is P2, but per the docs-authoring\n134\t   priority exception the docs epic derives its priority from the strategy\n135\t   frontmatter (`priority: Critical`) → P0. Flagged so the inversion against\n136\t   the HLR label is visible; it does not push priority upstream to\n137\t   implementations.\n138\t4. **External schedule risk**: lab turnaround and review-board cadence dominate\n139\t   the schedule (per the strategy's own note); the tiered delivery above\n140\t   mitigates by decoupling Tier 1 value from the certification timeline.\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87404b102bc2cfb2","agent_id":"a9a21c328c388a183","session_id":"f6f494ff-e064-4d81-8a07-c93e866aadc4","uuid":"a986f829-3dab-4e86-8af0-5331d4653592","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:03:27.269Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-acd996a2abb5eba5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
