{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a05bfae19f7403da","type":"tool_result","content":"skills/epic-decompose/:\nprompts\nSKILL.md\n\nskills/epic-decompose/prompts/:\ndecompose-agent.md\nfetch-agent.md\nreview-agent.md\nrevise-agent.md\nskills/epic-decompose/prompts/review-agent.md:59:Check: Trace the dependency graph. Verify each edge against the DAG construction rules (boundary rules 1-3, investigation edges 4-5, implementation type ordering 6-12, implementation edges 13-16, external dependency edges 17-19, generation rules 20-23, AC rules 24-26). Check that parallel-eligible work (different repos, no shared artifacts) is not unnecessarily serialized. **Implementation-type parallelism (rules 7, 8, 10) — enumerate and check every pair:** epics whose `implementation_type` pairing is mandated parallel must NOT have a blocking edge between them in either direction. Check **every** `konflux-onboarding` epic against **every** general-implementation epic (a decomposition often has more than one general epic — e.g. a component controller AND an OLM/CSV packaging epic; check all of them, not just the most obvious one). Specifically, a `konflux-onboarding → general implementation` edge (rule 10), `license-validation → repo-onboarding` (rule 7), or `license-validation → konflux-onboarding` (rule 8) is a **critical** issue — score this criterion 0. The only permitted coupling between a `konflux-onboarding` epic and its component's general implementation is the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion, never a `dependencies`/DAG edge. Do not accept a rationale that the code \"needs the pipeline first.\" **In particular, an edge justified only by an image digest / SHA / `RELATED_IMAGE` / endpoint URL is a configuration reference (Rule 13), which must be an AC gate, not a `dependencies` edge — flag it as critical, do not accept it as an \"artifact dependency.\"** **Conditional branch files (`{ID}-BRANCH-<letter>-E*.md`), wh