{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b06d0a3b4252c66a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition — RHAISTRAT-9013: FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tStep 0 checks did not fire. The strategy is not below-threshold: it spans two\n15\tcomponents (KServe, Platform Operator) and multiple architecturally distinct\n16\twork streams (image remediation, CI enforcement, compliance evidence assembly\n17\tand external submission, documentation). It is not documentation-only: image\n18\tand code changes are required. Full decomposition follows.\n19\t\n20\t## Parsed Strategy Structure\n21\t\n22\t- Affected Components: KServe, Platform Operator (no owner teams stated)\n23\t- HLRs: HLR-1 (P0, all serving-stack images run on FIPS-enabled clusters with\n24\t  validated crypto), HLR-2 (P0, compliance evidence package assembled and\n25\t  submitted through the security review board to the external certification\n26\t  lab), HLR-3 (P1, CI gating check for FIPS regressions), HLR-4 (P2,\n27\t  documentation of FIPS support posture)\n28\t- Out of scope: FIPS posture for workbenches/pipelines/training, Common\n29\t  Criteria certification\n30\t- Open questions: none on scope; lab scheduling and review-board cadence are\n31\t  externally controlled\n32\t\n33\tMissing sections (health warning): no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n34\ttable, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no Non-Functional Requirements,\n35\tno Staff Engineer Input. Decomposition proceeded with available information.\n36\t\n37\t## Component Mapping\n38\t\n39\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | In architecture context? | Notes |\n40\t|---|---|---|---|\n41\t| KServe | KServe | Yes (architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md