{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab68057613f00625","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E007\n3\ttitle: CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in Platform Operator builds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 0\n20\t  architecture_claims: -1\n21\tai_implementability: Medium\n22\tai_implementability_score: 1\n23\timplementation_type: null\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in Platform Operator builds\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tA gating CI check that fails any Platform Operator serving-stack build which\n35\treintroduces non-validated crypto usage. This extends FIPS regression\n36\tenforcement (HLR-3) to the Platform Operator side of the serving stack: KServe\n37\tbuilds are gated by the RHOAI Serving CI check, and this epic gates the\n38\tPlatform Operator build pipeline confirmed by the platform-status validation.\n39\tIt is owned by the team that owns that pipeline rather than being folded into\n40\tthe KServe check, so each gate lives with its component's build\n41\tinfrastructure.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Implement a detection mechanism that identifies non-validated crypto usage in\n46\t  built Platform Operator images and binaries (the detection approach from the\n47\t  KServe check may be reused where applicable — knowledge transfer, not an\n48\t  artifact dependency)\n49\t- Wire the check into the confirmed Platform Operator build pipeline as a\n50\t  gating step\n51\t- Fail builds on detection; report results clearly\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- The check runs on every Platform Operator serving-stack build in the\n56\t  confirmed build pipeline\n57\t- A Platform Operator build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage fails\n58\t  the gate\n59\t- The check passes on the remediated Platform Operator image baseline\n60\t- Gate results are visible in build output\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-3 (P1): CI enforces FIPS regressions with a gating check that fails any\n65\t  serving-stack build reintroducing non-validated crypto usage — this epic\n66\t  covers the Platform Operator builds in the serving stack; KServe builds are\n67\t  gated by the KServe CI check owned by RHOAI Serving\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ace5612da984093","agent_id":"acd2df83908752a59","session_id":"f6f494ff-e064-4d81-8a07-c93e866aadc4","uuid":"ac5c6853-b9d9-4391-893b-d868fe85f238","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:15:36.774Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab68057613f00625","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
